  "final_message": "The root cause was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. It filtered invoices on `status == \"opened\"`, but the real status is `\"open\"` (see `InvoiceStatus` in `models.py`). The filter never matched, so no invoice was ever picked up for retry. That left `next_attempt_at` in the past and the subscription stuck in `past_due`.\n\nI changed it to `\"open\"`. I didn't add a test for the retry path; the existing 24 tests pass and mypy is clean.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}\n```",
